+| 2026-11-05 | Retain the Appendix B `localhost` destination for RPC and promises. Trealla resolves its local listener; contained GNU routes only the local stateless endpoint through its trusted broker, preserving caller-fetched source and private databases. | Closes the reported implementation gap without restoring `Host:Port` terms or relaxing external peer egress restrictions. The controller/broker lease records budget and client identity; broker-derived continuation owners and controller credentials remain outside query workers. Development fix; release pins and public nodes are unchanged. |
 | 2026-11-05 | Browser promise references now belong to the runtime client context and can be collected/disposed across its main engine and Workers. Creator exit and shell replacement retain them; collector interruption releases only its claims. | Aligns promise ownership with Appendix B. Context closure retires promises and closes admission. The clean pinned release is deployed to N0–N6; real-browser checks exercise its served assets in both execution modes. |
 | 2026-11-04 | Runtime introspection enumerates five capabilities and uses `independent` or `cooperative` isolation values. Implementation identity is provided by diagnostics, not the language predicate. | Aligns the public API with Appendix B while retaining private browser dispatch for naming and statechart startup. |
 | 2026-11-04 | Adopt Appendix B URI atoms, strict Boolean options, ordered caller-side sources and initial statechart XML, common supervisor replies, independent numeric execution/HTTP deadlines, and the closed HTTP field schema. Headers use case-insensitive first-field precedence across aliases and UTF-8 values; source fetching never inherits them. | Author-directed common contracts replace runtime-specific acceptance and result differences. The contained GNU worker and broker are promoted together; pinned destinations, reserved identities and operator credentials retain their protection. |
diff --git a/Deployment/README.md b/Deployment/README.md
index caeb44d..7f56393 100644
--- a/Deployment/README.md
+++ b/Deployment/README.md
@@ -665,6 +665,13 @@ never configure source downloads. The broker independently validates fields;
 trusted identity fields and the pinned Host remain protected. Existing access,
 rate and resource policies still apply.
 
+The development `localhost` repair adds one broker route for `rpc` and
+`promise`: the fixed local stateless `/call` endpoint. It grants no arbitrary
+loopback or source access. Root-owned leases carry the originating client
+identity and IP budget; the broker derives continuation owners and supplies
+controller credentials without passing them to workers. The controller and
+broker must be promoted together. This repair is not yet in the release pins.
+
 All public `/portal` and `/portal/` requests permanently redirect to
 `/demonstrator`, preserving their query string. Current links use `/demonstrator`.
 
